NODE id=matrix/executor/mcp.Manager.Spawn kind=method
  digest=b3:9874358213826d08408d044cf87d82dfb6757960e56d676001e3afda3b830144 file=executor/mcp/manager.go range=125:177 lang=go exported=true byte_range=4310:5734
  sig=func (m *Manager) Spawn(ctx context.Context, spec ServerSpec) (*Client, error)
  doc=Spawn launches an MCP server, runs the initialize handshake, and\nvalidates the tool manifest (Q21). On success, the server is\nregistered under its alias and ready for ToolsCall.\n\nSpawn is idempotent: spawning an alias that's already running is a\nno-op (returns the existing client). To replace, call Stop first.
